**One **– The accused was an employer at the relevant time;

**Two **– There was a risk from the conduct of the accused’s undertaking to the health and safety of non-employees;

**Three **– The accused failed to do something which would have eliminated or reduced that risk;

**Four **– It was reasonably practicable in the circumstances to have taken steps to eliminate or reduce that risk.

If you find that any of these elements have not been proven beyond reasonable doubt, then you must find NOA **not guilty** of failing to eliminate risks to the health of safety of non-employees.

